    "terrainName": "basic-desert",
    "description": "What: a civilian car that STOPS ON ITS OWN at the checkpoint's signal (CE-4622, R-2133's follow-up; docs/designs/vehicle-tactics/DESIGN_Checkpoint_And_Ramming.md CP-2, CP-3) on basic-desert: the squad 'Checkpoint' (Stopper, Searcher 1, Searcher 2, Rifleman, Gunner with an M249) runs Checkpoint on the 'Checkpoint approach' route (stop line x 380). A Neutral 'Car' with its 'Driver' drives east from x 100 to x 700 at 12 m/s — its route runs straight THROUGH the checkpoint, nothing authored slows it. The Stopper's signal asks it to stop (StopAtSignal, a reaction): it slows, stops at the line, is searched and released, and drives on along its route. Judge: (1) the Stopper signals (2) the car takes StopAtSignal (3) it reads ROUTINE (4) the Driver gets out with his hands up, the car is searched and RELEASED (5) the car drives on past x 500 after the release (6) nobody fires, never a threat. Check: scripts/scenario-regression.sh cp-civilian-stops"
